.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- collect file lines containing a substring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <myfilefunctions.h>

int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep
reads from the current position of
.I fp
to end-of-file and finds lines containing
.IR search_str .
Matching is case-sensitive. It allocates a copy of each matching line and
stores the copies in the array returned through
.IR matches .
The caller must free every copied line and then the array itself. If no
line matches,
.I *matches
is NULL. An empty search string matches every line.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines, or -1 for a NULL argument,
allocation failure, or stream read error.
